'' CONST and STATIC on a definition must agree with the declaration (fbc 217/218 -- one the
'' declaration lacked is refused, one it had may be repeated or left off); 'let', 'cast',
'' '[]' and the compound assignments are members or nothing (152) while a free binary '+'
'' and a free '->' are legal; a field of a const variable cannot be written (119); at a
'' call, a base pointer to a 'byval as D ptr' is 24 and a base value to a 'byref as D' is
'' 58; and 'type U extends object' inside a SUB is 263 with no method declared at all.
'' Matches fbc on lines 54, 56, 58, 60, 62, 63 and 64; the nested type reports on its
'' 'type' line (66) where fbc reports on the 'end type' (68).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/member-and-call-rules.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' GOLDEN: expected/member-and-call-rules.out
